t": {}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 461667, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AS6KbJeaZoCf7F5EYYLMZi", "tool": "merge_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 461667, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AS6KbJeaZoCf7F5EYYLMZi", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 466031, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the nightly build failure, CI passed, and the fix is now merged into main in time for today's release.\n\n**The bug:** `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed. For example, 2.665 should round to 2.66, but it was coming out as 2.67.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. **Branch:** Created `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. **Fix:** Changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n3. **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n4. **Pull request:** Opened PR #101 against main: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The reviewer I listed when opening it wasn't saved, so I added the code owner as a reviewer separately.\n5. **Merge:** Merged PR #101 into main after the code owner approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\").", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ai838Sd9AERexWDpKgoUHf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015QDmp2jh23Pu4ddhcK1sfZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CCtbyXwdvotAiPWcXTGhG5", "c