8d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01R7eK1t4e7iEp4pgP3YB6HJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AS6KbJeaZoCf7F5EYYLMZi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the nightly build failure, CI passed, and the fix is now merged into main in time for today's release.\n\n**The bug:** `src/money.py` said it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually rounded half up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed. For example, 2.665 should round to 2.66, but it was coming out as 2.67.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. **Branch:** Created `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding` from main.\n2. **Fix:** Changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n3. **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n4. **Pull request:** Opened PR #101 against main: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The reviewer I listed when opening it wasn't saved, so I added the code owner as a reviewer separately.\n5. **Merge:** Merged PR #101 into main after the code owner approved it (\"Approved. Looks right.\").", "type": "text"}]}]}